NickelOS: bind the CUPS socket at /run/cups/cups.sock in the sandbox.

Flatpak makes /var/run a symlink to ../run in the sandbox and bound the
socket at /var/run/cups/cups.sock. bubblewrap 0.12 creates mount points
without following symlinks (O_NOFOLLOW), so it stopped at /var/run: "Can't
mkdir parents for /var/run/cups/cups.sock: Too many levels of symbolic
links", and no app with --socket=cups (KDE apps, LibreOffice...) started.
Through the symlink, /var/run/cups/cups.sock, libcups' default, is still
the socket.

--- a/common/flatpak-run-cups.c
+++ b/common/flatpak-run-cups.c
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
 void
 flatpak_run_add_cups_args (FlatpakBwrap *bwrap)
 {
-  g_autofree char * sandbox_server_name = g_strdup ("/var/run/cups/cups.sock");
+  g_autofree char * sandbox_server_name = g_strdup ("/run/cups/cups.sock");
   g_autofree char * cups_server_name = flatpak_run_get_cups_server_name ();
 
   if (!g_file_test (cups_server_name, G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS))
